# Build a squared rectangle backwards from a polyhedral graph.
# This is the skeleton of the tetragonal anti-wedge: six corners, ten edges.
# One edge becomes the battery, every other edge becomes a wire with
# resistance one, and the current through each wire is the side of a square.
.view both
title Tetragonal anti-wedge as a Smith diagram

battery a e
a - b - c - d - a
a - f - e
b - f
c - e - d
